      "description": "Square screenshot in a ringed frame with the name below, outside the frame.",
      "html": "<a class=\"ds-tile\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-tile-frame\"><span class=\"ds-tile-image\"></span></span><span class=\"ds-tile-name\">Zutun.io</span><span class=\"ds-tile-desc\">Sitio con captura real.</span></a>",
      "css": ".ds-tile{display:block;max-width:320px;color:var(--primary);text-decoration:none;font-family:var(--font-sans,\"DM Sans Variable\",sans-serif);}.ds-tile-frame{display:block;overflow:hidden;border-radius:16px;box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--border)}.ds-tile-image{display:block;aspect-ratio:1;background:var(--muted);transition:transform .5s ease-out}.ds-tile-name{display:block;margin-top:12px;font-family:var(--font-display,\"Space Grotesk Variable\",sans-serif);font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:500;transition:color .15s}.ds-tile-desc{display:block;margin-top:4px;font-size:.875rem;color:var(--muted-foreground)}.ds-tile:hover .ds-tile-frame{box-shadow:0 0 0 2px var(--brand)}.ds-tile:hover .ds-tile-name{color:oklch(.47 .21 259)}.ds-tile:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--brand);outline-offset:2px;}:host-context(.dark) .ds-tile:hover .ds-tile-name{color:oklch(.72 .16 256)}@media (prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){.ds-tile:hover .ds-tile-image{transform:scale(1.02)}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Signed Index",
    "overview": "A plain, exact catalogue of real work with one person's signature on it. Near-white paper or near-black ground, type doing the structuring, hairlines doing the dividing, and a single electric cobalt that marks whatever can be acted on. Density is relaxed between sections and tight inside them: long pages made of ruled rows rather than cards.\n\nThe system stays out of the way of the material it presents: a portrait, screenshots of shipped sites, install commands. Those carry their own colour; the interface does not compete. Depth is almost absent, and motion is limited to colour changes on state and one quiet entrance. Both themes are first-class, and every cobalt decision is made twice because the accent changes lightness between them.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One chromatic accent, swapped in lightness per theme",
      "Space Grotesk names things; DM Sans explains them",
      "Hairline rules instead of cards and shadows",
      "Pill actions at a 44px target",
      "Typographic rows wherever no real image exists"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Cobalt Rule",
        "body": "Cobalt is the only hue the interface itself uses. Screenshots, the portrait and syntax highlighting bring their own colour; the failed copy state is the single exception inside the chrome.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cobalt Swap Rule",
        "body": "Accent text uses `brand-strong` on light and `brand-dark` on dark, always as a pair. `brand-strong-dark` is too pale to be the dark accent and is reserved for the primary pill's hover.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Baked Ground Rule",
        "body": "The portrait's cobalt is in the pixels, so it does not follow the theme. A replacement portrait must keep this ground, and no surface should try to match it with a theme variable, because `brand-strong` changes in dark mode and the raster does not.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "If it names something, it is Space Grotesk. If it explains something, it is DM Sans. Non-heading names must set the display face explicitly, because only h1 to h3 receive it automatically.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "No text in the system is uppercase or positively tracked. Hierarchy comes from size, weight and face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sticky Rail Rule",
        "body": "A home section is a heading rail plus content, not a centred stack. New sections take this shape unless they have a stated reason not to.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline Over Shadow Rule",
        "body": "To separate things, draw a 1px rule. Surfaces, rows and images never gain a shadow, and hover answers with colour or a ring rather than lift.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Radius Ladder Rule",
        "body": "Choose the radius by object size from the existing steps. Only pill actions and badges are fully round.",
        "section": "shapes"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Primary Rule",
        "body": "An action group holds at most one primary pill, and most groups hold none. The footer, tool rows and project pages run entirely on default pills.",
        "section": "components"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 44px Target Rule",
        "body": "Pills, nav links, icon buttons, the copy button and the footer email are at least 44px tall. Company links reach it through padding; links inside running text and the wordmark are not held to it.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do pair accent text as `brand-strong` on light and `brand-dark` on dark, every time.",
      "Do separate rows and sections with a 1px hairline in `border` / `border-dark`.",
      "Do build pills, nav links and icon buttons at 44px, with the shared 2px cobalt focus outline at 2px offset.",
      "Do set names that are not headings in the display face explicitly.",
      "Do build new home sections on the sticky rail and the 1fr to 2fr split from 1024px.",
      "Do keep a new portrait on the same flat `portrait-ground` backdrop.",
      "Do use a typographic row when a tool has no real capture, and a real capture when it does."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't introduce a second interface hue; red is reserved for the failed copy state, and cobalt covers everything else.",
      "Don't use `brand-strong-dark` for dark accent text, or match the portrait with a theme variable.",
      "Don't add shadows to surfaces, rows or images, or use lift as a hover response.",
      "Don't wrap content in cards when a hairline row will do.",
      "Don't put more than one primary pill in an action group.",
      "Don't draw window chrome on code: no fake title bars or traffic lights.",
      "Don't stand in a drawn mockup or placeholder where a real screenshot does not exist.",
      "Don't set labels in uppercase or tracked caps, and don't add a small label above a heading.",
      "Don't use a typeface beyond Space Grotesk, DM Sans and the code stack."
    ]
  }
}
